LiminalNet Community License — Development Draft 0.1
Copyright 2026 RZU Informatique

This draft records the intended distribution terms. Review it before a public
release. It is a source-available license, not an OSI-approved open-source license.

1. Permission
You may use LiminalNet without charge for personal, educational and internal
business purposes. You may inspect, copy, modify and redistribute the original
code and derivative versions without charge, subject to the conditions below.

2. Attribution
Retain this license, copyright notices and third-party notices in source and
binary distributions. Derivative versions must clearly state that they are
based on LiminalNet by RZU Informatique and identify that changes were made.
Do not imply endorsement by RZU Informatique or OpenAI.

3. Free distribution
You may not sell LiminalNet or derivative versions, require payment or a paid
subscription to access them, or incorporate a substantial portion of this code
into software distributed only for payment without separate written permission
from RZU Informatique. Internal use by a business is permitted. Independent paid
consulting or support is permitted if access to the software does not require
buying that service. Voluntary donations are permitted and must not unlock
exclusive software features or access.

4. Derivative versions
When redistributing modified versions, provide their corresponding source under
these same terms. Preserve recipients' rights to use, modify and share freely.

5. Third-party components
These terms apply only to code and original assets for which RZU Informatique
can grant these permissions. Third-party libraries, databases and other works
retain their own licenses and rights. See LICENSES/ and dependency metadata.
These terms do not revoke rights granted separately by third-party authors.

6. Warranty and liability
To the extent permitted by applicable law, the software is provided "AS IS",
without warranty of any kind. The authors are not liable for claims or damages
arising from its use. Mandatory statutory rights are not excluded.

7. Termination
Permissions under this license are conditional on compliance. If a violation is
corrected within 30 days of written notice, permissions are reinstated unless
the violation is repeated. No trademark rights are granted.
